# UML sequence (simplified): how two retry layers multiplied load on the saturated load balancers. GitHub, Aug 17, 2026.
# Hop order is didactic: GitHub's RCA does not publish the exact call path. Attempt counts (x3) are ILLUSTRATIVE.
...@_style
direction: down
seq: "UML sequence (simplified): two retry layers, Aug 17, 2026" {
  shape: sequence_diagram
  style.fill: "#0B1020"
  style.font-color: "#4CC9F0"
  client: "client\n(editor extension)" {class: warn}
  gw: "GitHub gateway" {class: focus}
  lb: "internal LB\n(HAProxy, flows exhausted)" {class: bad}
  auth: "auth /\nCopilot Token Service" {class: svc}
  client -> gw: "1. token request"
  gw -> lb: "2. auth call"
  lb -> auth: "3. slow (LB saturated)"
  gw -> gw: "4. timeout"
  layer1: "loop · layer 1: gateway retries (optimistic), up to 3 attempts (illustrative)" {
    style.fill: "#1A1424"; style.stroke: "#FFB803"; style.font-color: "#FFB803"
    gw -> lb: "retry, same LB"
  }
  gw -> client: "5. error / slow response"
  layer2: "loop · layer 2: client retry bug (latent, triggered by delayed replies)" {
    style.fill: "#101C2C"; style.stroke: "#4CC9F0"; style.font-color: "#4CC9F0"
    client -> gw: "retry"
    gw -> lb: "x3 again"
  }
  (** -> **)[*].style: {stroke: "#8C9EBF"; font-color: "#E6EDF7"; stroke-width: 2; italic: false}
}
note: |md
  **Worst case:** client 3 × gateway 3 = 9 calls per click (illustrative).

  **GitHub's real figure:** Copilot Token Service 7–9K → 70–100K requests/s (about 10×).

  Sources: githubstatus.com incident RCA; GitHub availability report (Aug 2026). CC BY 4.0 · Systems, Drawn
| {style.font-color: "#E6EDF7"}
seq -> note: {style.opacity: 0}
